  "pipeline": {
    "bake": "Cycles CPU, 1024 square, 12-sample assembled contact AO, component-isolated selected-to-active projection. Four continuous axial charts and four planar disks cover both LODs. The matching low physical finish with assembled AO supplies the four PBR roles where projection misses the carrier or crosses hard edges.",
    "maps": "Four standalone 1024 px PNGs and KTX-Software 4.4.2 UASTC KTX2 mip chains, rd orientation. Both exact formats embedded in each GLB. Base color and emission are sRGB. Tangent normals and packed AO/roughness/metalness are linear.",
    "determinism": "Two clean Blender 5.2.2 Linux x86_64 CPU generations, three threads, with independent KTX 4.4.2 encodes. Geometry reports, both geometry buffers and source glTF JSONs, all four PNGs, all four KTX2s and both self-contained GLBs matched byte for byte. Editable source archive hashes identify the delivered build.",
    "render": "Blender 5.2.2 LTS EEVEE on Apple Metal. 624 px square, 16 samples, AgX, shared studio. Source and both decoded KTX2 LODs share verified camera transforms in isometric, front, underside and top views."
  },
  "corrections": [
    "An automatic UV unwrap produced 14 invalid tangent normals. A profile-driven unwrap uses four continuous circumference charts with at least five texels per profile station and a separate UV disk for each cap.",
    "A high-source mesh intersection audit revealed 36 crossing triangle pairs at the four outside seams. A smooth, monotonic radial change and vertical clearance keep the titanium lip above the lens at every station. The final verifier checks the exact GLBs, the editable high shell, and the UV overlap of both LODs together.",
    "The first EEVEE comparison exposed metallic triangular patches on the coarse ceramic shoulder. A separate Cycles finish-ID projection identifies cross-material rays and supplies the correct low-face material at those texels, preserving assembled AO. The final verification probes the decoded metallic channel on every shoulder triangle."
  ],
